# Keep build inputs, keep secrets and history out of the image.
#
# Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file the production image carried
# .env (every credential the app has) and the whole .git history. Nothing in
# here is needed at build or run time:
#   - dotenv-rails is a development/test gem and BUNDLE_WITHOUT drops it, so
#     .env is never even read in the image.
#   - node_modules and public/packs are deliberately NOT ignored: webpacker
#     compiles assets during the build from the context.

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
config/master.key
config/credentials/*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.key

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local and editor state
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
*.swp

# Runtime and build leftovers
log/*
tmp/*
storage/*
coverage
.byebug_history
yarn-error.log
yarn-debug.log*
stats.json

# Docker's own files
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Docs and scratch
docs
plans
*.md
